# meta::dateModified = 2018-08-29
# meta::genre = academic
# meta::salientEntities = 77 (5*), 163 (5*), 172 (4*), 2 (3*), 42 (3), 51 (3*), 206 (3*), 13 (2), 14 (2), 47 (2*), 66 (2), 121 (2), 165 (2), 177 (2), 212 (2), 43 (1), 44 (1), 48 (1), 89 (1), 134 (1), 155 (1), 162 (1), 179 (1), 184 (1), 191 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0202223
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human) This paper presents a Web crawler-based computer system for automatically generating census data for an academic field, which is applied to the compilation of a census of faculty in Computer Science.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) This paper introduces an automated web crawling system that can efficiently collect comprehensive census data of academic faculty in any field, with a demonstration in computer science that enables studies of workforce diversity and dynamics over time.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) This article introduces a novel web crawler system designed to efficiently and accurately assemble a comprehensive census of academic fields from publicly available web data, which significantly reduces the time and labor involved in collecting faculty data by hand, enabling new research into faculty diversity, retention, and trends across disciplines.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) Researchers have developed a novel system to automatically assemble a census of an academic field using digital data from the public World Wide Web, providing a more accurate and efficient way to study the composition and diversity of the scientific workforce.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) A novel web-crawler system is introduced for efficiently and accurately assembling complete, longitudinal censuses of academic fields, enhancing research on workforce composition and diversity trends.
# meta::title = Automatically assembling a full census of an academic field
