# meta::genre = academic
# meta::salientEntities = 2 (5*), 3 (5*), 4 (5*), 28 (5*), 19 (4*), 55 (3), 77 (2), 152 (2), 5 (1), 31 (1), 32 (1), 37 (1), 51 (1*), 58 (1), 154 (1), 156 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://www.mdpi.com/2504-3900/21/1/43
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This paper presents a study of mutation operators, which simulate likely software errors for testing purposes, in the area of Geographic Information Systems (GIS).
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) This paper proposes new mutation operators designed specifically for testing Geographic Information Systems (GIS) applications by introducing artificial errors into the system and demonstrates their application on two real-world GIS cases.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) The article introduces mutation operators for testing Geographic Information Systems (GIS) and illustrates their application with case studies on real GIS applications, showing how these operators replicate common programming errors in GIS, and suggesting future expansions to other domains and enhancements in test case automation.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) This article proposes the definition of specific mutation operators for testing Geographic Information Systems (GIS) applications, which were applied to two real-world GIS applications to generate mutants and test their behavior.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) The authors propose and implement domain-specific mutation operators tailored for testing Geographic Information Systems (GIS), demonstrating their effectiveness through applications in real-world GIS software, and suggest extending this approach to other domains.
# meta::title = Design of Mutation Operators for Testing Geographic Information Systems
