# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeanne_Moreau
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) Jeanne Moreau was an award winning French actress, singer, screenwriter and director, best known for starring in the films Elevator to the Gallows (1958) and Jules et Jim (1962).
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) French actress Jeanne Moreau (1928-2017) had an illustrious career spanning 1947-2012, winning major awards including a BAFTA Fellowship and César Award, while working with renowned directors and establishing herself as a leading figure in French cinema and theater.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) Jeanne Moreau, a celebrated French actress, singer, and filmmaker, known for iconic roles in “Elevator to the Gallows” and “Jules et Jim,” earned awards like Cannes Best Actress, a César, and a BAFTA Fellowship, and collaborated with renowned directors such as Louis Malle and François Truffaut.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) Jeanne Moreau was a French actress, singer, screenwriter, and director who was active in the film industry from 1947 to 2012, winning numerous awards for her performances in films such as “Seven Days... Seven Nights” and “Jules et Jim”.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Jeanne Moreau was a prominent French actress, singer, screenwriter, and director whose career spanned seven decades, including notable roles in films like “Elevator to the Gallows” and “Jules et Jim,” and she received numerous accolades throughout her illustrious career.
