# meta::sourceURL = https://www.linguistics.ucsb.edu/research/santa-barbara-corpus#SBC001
# meta::speakerCount = 3
# meta::summary1 = (human1) Mae Lynne tells about her experiences studying horse anatomy and blacksmithing in college in order to be able to take care of horses.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) The speaker discusses their experience learning horse hoof trimming and farrier work in college, including studying horse anatomy, practicing with pre-made horseshoes, and their ongoing concerns about properly trimming hooves.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) The speaker discusses their experiences with horse trimming and shoeing, emphasizing the educational process and the specialized knowledge needed, expressing apprehension about causing harm and noting the rarity of female farriers in practice, while highlighting the importance of understanding tendons, ligaments, bones, and the white line guide in hoof trimming.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) A person is discussing with Mae Lynne the process of trimming horses' hooves, which requires knowledge of anatomy and equipment, and is worried about making a mistake and potentially causing harm to the horse.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct; postedited) The narrator describes their experience learning to trim horse hooves, including the extensive anatomical knowledge required and their lingering fear of potentially harming the animal.
# meta::title = Actual Blacksmithing
