# meta::summary1 = (human1) Mitchell Roberts is suing Matthew Collins for roughly $700 after Matthew hired him and his workers to do a carpet job at UCSB, for which he had allegendly promised to pay the workers' full wages, but refused to pay 26% of their pay comprising unemployment insurance and social security.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) In a small claims hearing, Mitchell Roberts sues Matthew Collins of ABC Builders Interiors over disputed payroll deductions, claiming Collins failed to cover the agreed-upon 26% employer contribution costs when processing wages for Roberts' employees on a state-funded carpet installation project at UCSB.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) In a dispute over a $700 payment, Mitchell Roberts claims Matthew Collins and ABC Builders Interiors agreed to cover employee costs to allow him to profit from a carpet installation project, but Collins argues that Roberts misunderstood the contract terms, which included a 26% deduction for employer contributions.
# meta::summary4 = (Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct) A contractor, Mitchell Roberts, sues employer Matthew Collins for $700 in unpaid labor costs, alleging Collins failed to pay employees' wages as agreed upon.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) A dispute arises between Mitchell Roberts, a licensed contractor, and Matthew Collins regarding unpaid labor costs for installing carpet at UCSB, with Roberts claiming Collins agreed to cover the employer contribution while Collins maintains the arrangement was entirely verbal and denies owing additional payments.
