# newdoc id = GUM_essay_sexlife
# global.Entity = GRP-etype-infstat-salience-centering-minspan-link-identity
# meta::author = Miri Forbes; Nicholas Eaton; Robert Krueger
# meta::dateCollected = 2023-09-05
# meta::dateCreated = 2023-09-06
# meta::dateModified = 2023-09-11
# meta::genre = essay
# meta::salientEntities = 2 (5*), 43 (4*), 3 (3), 105 (3), 106 (3), 5 (2*), 6 (2*), 7 (2*), 36 (2), 54 (2), 82 (2*), 92 (2*), 135 (2*), 137 (2*), 139 (2), 141 (2), 154 (2), 32 (1*), 60 (1), 83 (1), 103 (1), 104 (1), 116 (1), 119 (1), 138 (1), 144 (1), 145 (1), 149 (1), 152 (1*), 158 (1), 159 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://openwa.pressbooks.pub/lwtech88readings/
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This essay challenges the notion that aging is associated with a decline in sex life, instead showing that older adults' priorities and sexual experiences contribute to a better sexual quality of life by drawing on a longitudinal study by Dr. Miri Forbes, Dr. Nicholas Eaton, and Dr. Robert Kruegerdata with data from 6,000 individuals spanning ages 20-93.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) According to research analyzing data from 6,000 Americans over 18 years, older adults who prioritize quality over quantity in their sex lives and maintain similar levels of engagement as younger people actually report better sexual satisfaction, suggesting that sexual wisdom develops with age and life experience.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) Research by Forbes, Eaton, and Krueger suggests that sexual quality of life often improves with age, as older adults prioritize quality over frequency, benefiting from life experience and strong romantic relationships, leading to enhanced sexual satisfaction and overall well-being.
# meta::summary4 = (Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct) The quality of sexual life actually improves for many individuals with age, as they develop a greater emphasis on relationship quality, intimacy, and partner pleasure, and this positive pattern holds even when controlling for physical and mental health declines.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Despite common perceptions, older adults often maintain or even enhance their sexual satisfaction through life experience, prioritizing quality over quantity, and developing greater knowledge and understanding of their own and their partner's preferences.
# meta::title = 28: Why Sex Gets Better in Older Age
# newpar
# newpar_block = head (1 s)
# sent_id = GUM_essay_sexlife-1
