# meta::summary1 = (human1) After torrential rain floods their house and garden, some people are swept away to sea amid mermaids and a whale, and climb aboard a galleon with singing sailors, where they meet the captain of the ship.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022; postedited) A rainstorm in a garden escalates into a fantastical flood where the protagonists witness mermaids, sea creatures, and a mysterious “He” while being swept from their porch to a whale's back and finally rescued aboard a magical galleon.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) A sudden rain turns a garden into a flood filled with mythical creatures and prophetic whispers, as the narrator and companions embark on a surreal journey atop a whale before being rescued by a mysterious galleon whose crew chants about an anticipated figure, leaving them amidst storm and fantasy.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) A family sits on their porch as a storm rages outside, and they wait for the arrival of a mythical being known as “He”, accompanied by singing mermaids and a whale, as welll as a galleon and its captain.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct; postedited) In this descriptive passage, the narrator vividly recounts an intense storm that engulfs their garden, transforming it into a chaotic aquatic environment filled with rising earthworms, playful fish, and mysterious oceanic creatures like whales and mermaids, culminating in a dramatic rescue aboard a ship.
