# meta::sourceURL = http://smallbeerpress.com/wp-content/uploads/Rosenbaum_Ant_King.pdf
# meta::speakerCount = 2
# meta::summary1 = (human1) A poor woman who lost her husband and four children in a war hears about the valley of giants from a traveller at a bar and, after spending a night with her, decides to pack for a journey.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) A grandmother in a war-torn city, having lost her family except for an estranged granddaughter, follows a mysterious traveler's implicit lead toward a “valley of giants” after encountering her in a waterfront bar frequented by fellow grandmothers.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) After losing her family to war and tragedy, an elderly woman living in a city predominantly inhabited by grandmothers encounters a mysterious traveler who speaks of giants, prompting her to leave her desolate home with packed essentials in search of something beyond the bleakness of her current existence.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) A woman reflects on her life after the war, remembering her parents, husband, and children, and her granddaughter, and then encounters a mysterious traveler who speaks of the Valley of Giants, a place where the old and the vulnerable still hold on to their dignity and pride.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) After burying her loved ones during wartime, a grandmother embarks on a journey to find a valley of giants, guided by a mysterious traveler, leaving behind her home and possessions in search of companionship and purpose.
