# meta::sourceURL = http://www.rifters.com/real/Blindsight.htm
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) Siri tells about an incident from his childhood, when, after recovering from brain surgery to treat epilepsy, he saved his friend Pag from bullies hitting him by brutally beating three of them with a rock.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) A young boy who had half his brain removed to treat epilepsy violently defends his only friend from bullies, leading his friend to claim he's no longer the same person since the surgery.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) A young boy named Siri, altered by brain surgery to manage his epilepsy, recounts a pivotal moment from his childhood when he instinctively defended his best friend Robert “Pag” Paglino from bullies, showcasing his struggles with empathy and identity as his friend accuses him of being changed or replaced by the procedure.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) The narrator recalls the day his best friend, Robert Paglino, was attacked by a group of older kids at the playground, and he, the narrator, intervened to defend him, but in doing so, he reveals a new aspect of himself that he didn't know existed.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) The narrator, reflecting on a pivotal moment from childhood, recounts helping his genetically modified friend Robert “Pag” defend himself against bullies, which leads to the narrator's own transformation after the incident.
# meta::title = Blingsight, Prologue
