# meta::summary1 = (human1) Jellicoh College student Rachel Rook speaks with her boyfriend Carroll, whom she met a few months earlier at Jellicoh College library where he works, about meeting her parents for the first time on the farm where they live together.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022; postedited) A young graduate student falls for a mysterious 19-year-old college student when she returns a damaged book to his library desk one day, then spends two months dating her before finally being invited to meet her parents at the family farm.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) The reserved and organized Rachel Rook brings her boyfriend Carroll, whom she's impressed since they met at the Jellicoh College library, to meet her parents on their farm after previously keeping them apart, and while Carroll prepares diligently, Rachel warns him her mother might find him lacking seriousness.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) Carroll, a young man who has recently started a relationship with Rachel, goes to meet her parents, who are surprisingly open-minded and accepting, but also critical of his personality, revealing a lot about Rachel and her family's values.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Rachel takes Carroll, her boyfriend, to meet her parents for the first time, despite her reservations about introducing him due to her mother's disapproval of his laid-back personality.
