# meta::sourceURL = http://thepowerfactory.com/pivot/entry.php?id=28&w=thepowerfactory_1
# meta::speakerCount = 3
# meta::summary1 = (human1) A protagonist and his friend Pete try to get a fairy out of the protagonist's nose, and finally succeed when they realize that the protagonist can make a wish for the fairy to leave.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) A boy discovers a sarcastic fairy stuck in his nose while riding his bike and, with his friend Pete's help, manages to get rid of it by using one of his three wishes, though he never gets to use the remaining two.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) A boy believes he has a fairy stuck in his nose, which communicates with him and his friend Pete, until they convince it to leave by wishing it away, leaving the boy wondering about his remaining two wishes.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) Pete and his friend are trying to figure out how to get a fairy out of the friend's nose, with the fairy insulting and sarcastically remarking, until they come up with the idea that fairies give three wishes when caught, allowing them to release the fairy from the nose, but leaving the friend to wait for their remaining two wishes.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) A boy named Pete and the narrator have a conversation about a fairy stuck up the narrator's nose, which causes them to sneeze and creates a humorous situation.
# meta::title = Doesn't it make you just want to sneeze?
