# meta::author = Maureen F. McHugh
# meta::dateCollected = 2017-09-13
# meta::dateCreated = 2008-04-22
# meta::dateModified = 2008-04-22
# meta::genre = fiction
# meta::salientEntities = 2 (5*), 3 (5*), 12 (5*), 4 (4*), 16 (4*), 37 (4*), 23 (3), 33 (3), 55 (3*), 41 (2), 56 (2*), 10 (1), 27 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = http://smallbeerpress.com/wp-content/uploads/McHugh_Mothers.pdf
# meta::speakerCount = 2
# meta::summary1 = (human1) While gunfire can be heard outside, a protagonist on an extraterrestrial colony that had been forgotten by Earth spends a night with Veronique, the daughter of an anthropologist from Earth who is studying the rediscovered colony's people, before falling asleep and dreaming of being a hero on Earth.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) A tense nighttime conversation occurs between two characters, where a graduate student named Veronique reveals her anthropologist father's work studying Earth colony stories, while gunfire and chaos unfold outside.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) In a tense setting where gunfire interrupts the night, the narrator reflects on conversations with Veronique, an anthropology graduate student visiting from Earth with her father, an anthropologist interested in the history and stories of their world, and they both grapple with the disconnect between their cultures while Veronique seeks temporary escape from her circumstances.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) A young girl, Veronique, and her friend stay up late together, and Veronique shares with her friend that she is an offworlder, her father is an anthropologist, and she is studying history, including the history of their colony on her friend's world, and that they are here to learn about how people came there from Earth.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) In a shared nighttime conversation between the narrator and Veronique, who has traveled from Earth to a colonized planet, they discuss their backgrounds, cultural differences, and the history of the colony while the surrounding community experiences ongoing conflict.
