# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Interview_with_US_political_activist_and_philosopher_Noam_Chomsky
# meta::speakerCount = 2
# meta::summary1 = (human1) Michael Dranove interviews political activist, linguist and philosopher Noam Chomsky about the background of protests against the 60th NATO conference, as well as the revival of leftwing labor actions such as mass strikes in the US and around the world.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) MIT Professor Emeritus Noam Chomsky discusses NATO's continued existence after the Soviet collapse, questioning its purpose as a Western military alliance and shares thoughts on recent labor actions as potential signs of a Left revival.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) In a 2009 interview, Noam Chomsky questions NATO's relevance after the Soviet Union's fall and its eastward expansion, critiques its role in Western energy security, and discusses global labor strikes as potential signs of a leftist revival, highlighting a recent sit-down strike in the U.S.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) Noam Chomsky discusses his views on NATO and its relevance in the modern world, arguing that the alliance's continued existence is not justified and that its expansion and militarism are threats to Russia and other nations.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Noam Chomsky discusses the continued relevance and potential dangers of NATO's existence, questioning its original purpose and current role in global politics, while also touching on recent labor movements and their significance.
# meta::title = Interview with US political activist and philosopher Noam Chomsky
