# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Wikinews_interviews_New_York_bar_owner_on_Santorum_cocktail
# meta::speakerCount = 2
# meta::summary1 = (human1) Wikinews interviews Jonathan M. Stan, co-owner of the Pacific Standard bar in New York, about his Santorum Cocktail, which alludes to columnist Dan Savage's campaign to define 'santorum' as a frothy by-product of anal sex, in protest of comments made by former Pennsylvania Senator Rick Santorum against homosexuality.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) A Brooklyn bar owner created a cocktail named “Santorum” inspired by Dan Savage's neologism of Rick Santorum's name, featuring vodka, Baileys Irish Cream, and chocolate flakes, which gained media attention and popularity among customers.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) Wikinews interviews Jonathan M. Stan, co-owner of the Brooklyn-based Pacific Standard bar, about the popularity of the “Santorum” cocktail inspired by a satirical neologism from columnist Dan Savage, named after former Senator Rick Santorum, with increased customer interest in the cocktail following media coverage, despite its provocative origins.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) The Pacific Standard bar in Brooklyn, New York, created a Santorum cocktail in response to the satirical definition of the term coined by Dan Savage, inspired by Rick Santorum's comments on homosexuality.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) A New York City bar named Pacific Standard created a politically-themed cocktail called Santorum, which includes vodka, Baileys Irish Cream, and Angostura bitters, and is served with Godiva chocolate flakes, inspired by the neologism “santorum” created in response to Rick Santorum's comments about homosexuality.
