# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/BDSM_as_business:_An_interview_with_the_owners_of_a_dungeon
# meta::speakerCount = 3
# meta::summary1 = (human1) Two owners of a BDSM dungeon in New York talk about their business in an interview, explaining about how they choose who to hire, the costs of operating the business, and how it is advertised.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022; postedited) BDSM dungeon owners discusses business operations, startup costs, advertising challenges, and unique hiring practices, including a custom psychological test to ensure they employ educated, kind-hearted employees despite common misconceptions about the industry.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) In an interview, BDSM dungeon owners address industry misconceptions, stressing the need for an educated, pleasant staff to maintain a positive environment, and discuss the challenges and costs of their business, like advertising and rent, while adapting to changing attitudes toward adult content on advertising platforms.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) An interview with the owners of a dungeon reveals that their business is often misunderstood as being dark and evil, but in reality, they hire educated and nice people, and advertise in local papers and online, with a focus on the Internet as a safer way to reach customers.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) The owners of a BDSM business explain how they run their dungeon-style establishment, emphasizing that it is not what it is often portrayed as, and discuss their unique approach to hiring employees based on personality tests rather than physical appearance.
