# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Frank_Messina:_An_interview_with_the_%27Mets_Poet%27
# meta::speakerCount = 2
# meta::summary1 = (human1) In an interview in 2007, Frank Messina, known as the 'Mets Poet', recites a stanza from one of his poems and talks about how his poetry in support of the New York Mets baseball team has touched fans of the team.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) Poet Frank Messina discusses his unexpected fame as “The Mets Poet,” explaining how his baseball-themed poetry has attracted new fans and mainstream attention, though it represents only a portion of his extensive work that includes spoken word performances and 9/11-inspired pieces.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) Frank Messina, the 'Mets Poet,' discusses his career, highlighting global performances and the surprising impact of his New York Mets-inspired poetry among sports fans, which resonates with audiences on various levels, reflecting both personal and collective challenges, as well as drawing comparisons to historical figures like Walt Whitman.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) Frank Messina, a poet and spoken word artist, discusses his recent attention and praise for his Mets-inspired poetry, which he feels overshadows his previous work in poetry, but he finds it meaningful to have touched fans through his work.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Frank Messina, known as the “Mets Poet,” reflects on the impact of his baseball-inspired poetry on fans, including personal interactions and newfound recognition from those typically uninterested in poetry.
# meta::title = Frank Messina: An interview with the 'Mets Poet'
