# newdoc id = GUM_letter_gorbachev
# global.Entity = GRP-etype-infstat-salience-centering-minspan-link-identity
# meta::author = Nicolaus Tideman (signed by Nicolaus Tideman, William Vickrey, Mason Gaffney, Lowell Harriss, Jacques Thisse, Charles Goetz, Gene Wunderlich, Daniel R. Fusfeld, Carl Kaysen, Elizabeth Clayton, Robert Dorfman, Tibor Scitovsky, Richard Goode, Susan Rose-Ackerman, James Tobin, Richard Musgrave, Franco Modigliani, Warren J. Samuels, Guy Orcutt, Eugene Smolensky, Ted Gwartney, Oliver Oldman, Zvi Griliches, William Baumol, Gustav Ranis, John Helliwell, Giulio Pontecorvo, Robert Solow, Alfred Kahn, Harvey Levin)
# meta::dateCollected = 2023-09-06
# meta::dateCreated = 1990-11-07
# meta::dateModified = 1990-11-07
# meta::genre = letter
# meta::salientEntities = 31 (5*), 32 (5*), 64 (5*), 2 (4*), 6 (4*), 8 (4*), 9 (4*), 35 (4), 36 (4*), 1 (3*), 28 (3*), 3 (2), 15 (2*), 27 (2), 76 (2*), 10 (1), 18 (1*), 34 (1), 49 (1), 93 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Open_letter_to_Mikhail_Gorbachev_(1990)
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) In this open letter to President Mikhail Gorbachev of the Soviet Union, a group of economists applaud Soviet efforts to transition to a free market economy while also cautioning against private collection of rental payments for land, instead advocating for all citizens to pay rents to the government in exchange for public services and utilities.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) In a 1990 letter to Mikhail Gorbachev, a group of petitioners advise that while the USSR's move to a market economy is commendable, they should avoid privatizing land rents and instead collect them as government revenue to fund public services and ensure fair distribution of natural resources.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) In a 1990 letter to Mikhail Gorbachev, the authors praise the Soviet Union's shift towards a market economy but caution against privatizing land rent, advocating for its use as government revenue to ensure equitable land distribution, efficient public services funding, and to avoid economic pitfalls observed in other market economies.
# meta::summary4 = (Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct) A public revenue system should collect and redistribute the rent of land to promote efficient use of resources and ensure all citizens benefit equally from the value added by public services.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct; postedited) A group of people writes to Mikhail Gorbachev, outlining the importance of retaining the rent of land as a source of government revenue to ensure economic prosperity in the Soviet Union's transition to a market economy while avoiding potential pitfalls found in Western economic systems.
# meta::title = Open letter to Mikhail Gorbachev
