# meta::summary1 = (human1) On September 12, 2015, at least 107 people were killed and 238 wounded at Mecca's Grand Mosque in Saudi Arabia when a storm caused a construction crane to collapse just ten days before the beginning of the Hajj, Islam's annual pilgrimage to Mecca.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) A construction crane at Mecca's Grand Mosque collapsed during a storm, killing at least 107 people and injuring 238 just days before the annual Hajj pilgrimage, while the mosque was undergoing expansion work to improve crowd control.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) Saudi Arabia's Civil Defense reported that a crane collapse at Mecca's Grand Mosque on September 12, 2015, killed 107 and injured 238 just ten days before the Hajj pilgrimage, underscoring ongoing construction efforts to improve crowd control during the significant Muslim religious event.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) A crane collapsed into Mecca's Grand Mosque on September 12, 2015, killing at least 107 people and wounding 238, due to strong winds and heavy rain, just ten days before the start of the Hajj pilgrimage.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) A storm caused a crane to collapse in Mecca's Grand Mosque, resulting in at least 107 deaths and 238 injuries, occurring just before the start of the Hajj pilgrimage.
