# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Scientology_defector_arrested_after_attempting_to_leave_organization
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) On September 29, 2010, after leaving Scientology's elite Sea Org group and going to Florida to meet former scientologist Tom Devocht, 19 year old Daniel Montalvo was arrested in Los Angeles on charges of grand theft for allegedly taking Scientology hard drives and a zip drive when he defected.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) A 19-year-old lifelong Scientology member was arrested and charged with theft after leaving the elite Sea Org group with hard drives, following his disillusionment with the organization and attempted escape that led to interrogation by church officials.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) Former Sea Org member Daniel Montalvo was charged with grand theft for allegedly taking hard drives after leaving Scientology, leading to intense interrogation and alleged framing attempts by the Church, despite returning the property, while his legal defense has been backed by ex-Scientologists and fundraising efforts.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) Daniel Montalvo, a 19-year-old former member of the Sea Org, was arrested after leaving the organization and attempting to leave with computer hard drives, which Scientology officials claimed were stolen, and was released on $20,000 bail.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Former Sea Org member Daniel Montalvo was arrested by Scientology after he attempted to leave the organization and was accused of stealing hard drives, sparking controversy over the strict rules and control exercised by Scientology over its members.
