# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Pop_culture_celebrated_at_Fan_Expo_Canada_2016_in_Toronto
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) The 2016 Fan Expo in Toronto, Canada, was attended by thousands, including many cosplayers, with appearances from celebrities such as Stan Lee, Mark Hamill and Margaret Atwood, video game demos, an Esports championship and charity events.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) The 22nd Fan Expo Canada in Toronto attracted thousands of fans and featured celebrity guests like Stan Lee, Mark Hamill, and Margaret Atwood, along with gaming demonstrations, eSports tournaments, charity events, and numerous cosplayers displaying their handcrafted costumes.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) Fan Expo Canada 2016, at Metro Toronto Convention Centre, featured genres including sci-fi, horror, anime, fantasy and comics, with celebrities like Stan Lee and Mark Hamill attending and highlights including cosplay, gaming demos, and the Northern Arena Esports Championship, as well as charitable support provided by groups like 501st Legion and Comic Corps of Canada.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) The 22nd Fan Expo Canada took place at the Metro Toronto Convention Centre, attracting thousands of fans and featuring celebrity guests, vendors, and activities including cosplay, gaming, and charity events, with a focus on science fiction, horror, anime, fantasy, and comics.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Fan Expo Canada 2016 showcased a diverse range of pop culture attractions, featuring celebrity guest appearances, vendor booths, charitable events, and a vibrant array of cosplay, drawing thousands of enthusiasts to the Metro Toronto Convention Centre.
