# meta::summary1 = (human1) The government of New Zealand intends to hold two referendums to consider adopting a new national flag design, to replace the current one, which is partly based on the flag of the United Kingdom.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) New Zealand has initiated a public process to consider changing its national flag design, allowing citizens to propose ideas and vote in two referendums despite only 25% of the population currently supporting a change.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) The New Zealand government is considering a flag change, involving public design suggestions and input in two referendums, planned despite declining support at a cost of NZ$26 million, with the first vote on new designs from November 20 to December 11, and a final choice between the new and current flags in early 2016.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) The New Zealand government has begun a public process to consider changing the national flag, with the first meeting taking place in May and two referendums planned to reach a verdict on the flag's design, which is expected to cost NZ $26 million.
