# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Hackers_attack_Church_of_Scientology_website
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) Following the removal of a promotional video featuring Scientologist Tom Cruise from YouTube at the request of the Church of Scientology, hackers attacked the Scientology.org website, making it inaccessible for a number of days in January 2008.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) Anonymous hackers launched a successful attack on the Church of Scientology's website in retaliation for the church's attempts to remove a promotional Tom Cruise video from YouTube, causing the site to temporarily shut down.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) In January 2008, hackers posing as “Anonymous” attacked the Church of Scientology's website, allegedly due to its attempts to remove a Tom Cruise video from YouTube, which led to the site's temporary shutdown and ignited ongoing conflict between Internet activists and the Church, sparking debate over the implications of digital attacks.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) The Church of Scientology's website was attacked by hackers, led by the group “Anonymous”, in response to the Church's attempts to remove a promotional video featuring Tom Cruise from YouTube, causing the site to shut down, and critics of the Church of Scientology to criticize the attack, leading to an increase in traffic to the site.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct; postedited) Hackers associated with an online insurgency declared war on the Church of Scientology's website in response to the organization's efforts to remove a promotional video featuring Tom Cruise from YouTube.
# meta::title = Hackers attack Church of Scientology website
