# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Microsoft_waits_for_death_of_Internet_Explorer_6
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) With the development of its Internet Explorer 9 almost complete and stiff competition from Mozilla Firefox, Safari and Chrome, Microsoft has started a campaign to persuade users to stop using its older browser, the highly successful but now obsolete IE6, which they no longer want to support.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) Microsoft has launched an aggressive campaign to phase out Internet Explorer 6, its decade-old browser with numerous security vulnerabilities, as IE's market share drops and newer browsers gain popularity.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) Microsoft has launched “The Internet Explorer 6 Countdown,” a campaign urging users to transition from the outdated Internet Explorer 6 to newer versions, aiming to reduce its usage to below one percent due to the browser's declining market share, compatibility issues with modern web standards, and significant security vulnerabilities.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) Microsoft is ending support for Internet Explorer 6, a 10-year-old browser, and is urging users to upgrade to newer versions, such as Internet Explorer 9, due to its declining market share and security vulnerabilities.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Microsoft is pushing users to abandon the outdated and insecure Internet Explorer 6 in favor of more modern and secure browsers like IE9, Firefox, and Chrome.
# meta::title = Microsoft waits for death of Internet Explorer 6
