# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) After a series of anti-Pyongyang loudspeaker propaganda broadcasts from South to North Korea, artillery fire was exchanged between the two countries on August 20, 2015, leading to the evacuation of about 80 people in the South Korean town of Yeoncheon and placement of both countries' armies on high alert.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) After exchanging artillery fire with South Korea over propaganda loudspeakers at the border, North Korea placed its military in a “quasi-state of war” and threatened further military action if South Korea does not stop the broadcasts within 48 hours.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) After an artillery exchange, North Korea put its military on high alert and in a “quasi-state of war,” with Kim Jong-un ordering the army to prepare for battle over South Korea's propaganda broadcasts, which North Korea claims are a grave provocation, and North Korea threatening military retaliation if the broadcasts don't stop within 48 hours.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) North Korea has placed its military on high alert and ordered its troops to prepare for a “quasi-state of war” after exchanging artillery fire with South Korea, and has vowed to respond militarily within 48 hours if the South continues to broadcast anti-North propaganda.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) North Korea declared its military to be in a “quasi-state of war” following a recent exchange of artillery fire with South Korea, escalating tensions between the two nations.
# meta::title = North Korea puts military in 'quasi-state of war'
