# meta::salientEntities = 1 (5*), 2 (5*), 3 (5*), 7 (5*), 47 (5*), 11 (4*), 12 (4*), 42 (3), 6 (2*), 17 (2), 18 (2), 19 (2), 20 (2), 26 (2*), 29 (2*), 21 (1), 27 (1*), 56 (1*), 58 (1*), 59 (1*), 73 (1), 77 (1), 92 (1), 102 (1), 110 (1), 111 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikinews.org/wiki/Lantern_Festival_in_Taipei_lights_up_the_night
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This report describes the March 2007 Taipei City Lantern Festival in Taiwan, themed after the Chinese zodiac's year of the pig and set to host some six million vistors, which included lanterns representing the counties of Taiwan, lanterns made by student groups and lanterns from foreign countries in the 240,000 square meter Chiang Kai Shek Memorial park.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) Taipei's annual Lantern Festival kicked off at Chiang Kai-Shek Memorial with a massive light display featuring a 15-meter high rotating pig as centerpiece, drawing an expected 6 million visitors to celebrate the Chinese New Year tradition.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) The Taipei City Lantern Festival celebrates the end of the Chinese New Year and the Year of the Pig, featuring vibrant displays at Chiang Kai Shek Memorial, including a 15-meter high rotating pig, attracting millions, despite crowded public transport, with festivities running until March 11.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) The Taipei Lantern Festival in Taiwan's Chiang Kai Shek Memorial Park was a major event, attracting 6 million visitors and featuring colorful lantern scenes, a rotating pig, and a fog machine, with the crowds swelling on weekends but thinning out later in the festival.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) The Taipei City Lantern Festival, now in its 28th year, celebrates the Chinese New Year with colorful lantern displays, live performances, and cultural exhibits attracting millions of visitors annually.
# meta::title = Lantern Festival in Taipei lights up the night
