# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) A stampede during the 2006 Hajj pilgrimage in Mecca killed over 345 Muslim pilgrims at Jamarat Bridge when fallen luggage created a bottleneck during the ritual stoning of Satan, despite Saudi officials implementing various safety measures.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) Over 345 Muslim pilgrims were tragically killed in a stampede at the Jamarat Bridge during the annual Hajj pilgrimage near Mecca, Saudi Arabia, despite existing safety measures, due to a bottleneck triggered by luggage from a bus, marking another deadly incident at the religious site where thousands gather to fulfill one of Islam's five pillars.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) A stampede during the Hajj pilgrimage in Saudi Arabia on January 12, 2006, resulted in the deaths of over 345 Muslim pilgrims, making it one of the deadliest stampedes in the history of the Hajj.
