# meta::summary1 = (human1) In his inaugural address on August 14, 1947, Indian Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru speaks of India's painful past and his hopes for a future of freedom ending poverty, ignorance and disease in India while creating a prosperous, democratic and progressive nation.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) In his historic “Tryst with Destiny” speech marking India's independence in 1947, Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru celebrates the nation's freedom from British rule while calling for unity, progress and dedication to build a prosperous democratic India that serves all its citizens.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) In his August 14, 1947 inaugural address, Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru reflects on India's independence struggle, stressing the responsibilities of freedom, urging dedication to eradicating poverty, ignorance, and inequality, and calling for peace and global cooperation, honoring those who fought for a prosperous, democratic India.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) In his inaugural address, Indian Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru celebrates India's independence and freedom, and outlines his vision for the country's future, calling for the country to strive for a better life for all its citizens and to work towards a more just and equal society.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Indian Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru delivers an emotional and inspiring address on the eve of independence, promising to work towards ending poverty, ignorance, and inequality while urging unity and cooperation among Indians and with other nations.
