# meta::summary1 = (human1) On August 8, 1974, US President Richard Nixon announced his decision to resign due to the Watergate affair, resulting in Vice President Ford being sworn in as President the following day.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) In a historic resignation speech addressing Watergate, President Richard Nixon announced his decision to step down from the presidency, citing loss of congressional support and the need to put national interests ahead of personal vindication.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) In an address to the nation, President Richard Nixon announced his resignation from office effective August 9, 1974, due to the Watergate scandal undermining his political support in Congress, emphasizing his belief that resignation was in the nation's best interest and expressing confidence in Vice President Gerald Ford's ability to lead the country moving forward.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) In an address to the nation, President Nixon announces his decision to resign the office of President of the United States, effective at noon the following day, citing the lack of political support from Congress to carry out the duties of the office.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) US President Richard Nixon announces his resignation due to the Watergate scandal, recommending Vice President Gerald Ford to take over the presidency and urging national unity despite the bitter division caused by the situation.
# meta::title = Address to the Nation Announcing Decision To Resign the Office of President of the United States
