# meta::sourceURL = https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-philadelphia-dinner-sponsored-the-democratic-county-executive-committee
# meta::speakerCount = 1
# meta::summary1 = (human1) US President John F. Kennedy gives a speech in support of the mayor of Philadelphia and Democractic congressmen and senators, and details some of his administration's achievements and policy goals.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) President John F. Kennedy addresses Democrats in Philadelphia, expressing gratitude for their support in the 1960 campaign, highlighting local Democratic achievements, and discussing national economic progress including job growth and potential tax cuts to stimulate further expansion.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) In Philadelphia, the speaker, a proud Democrat, highlights strong local Democratic support, commends leaders for contributions, addresses economic growth and challenges like unemployment and high taxes, and emphasizes the potential benefits of a proposed tax cut for future expansion.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) A Democratic president speaks in Philadelphia, expressing pride and gratitude for the city's support during the 1960 presidential campaign and reporting on progress made in the country's goals, including increased economic growth and reduced unemployment.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Former U.S. President John F. Kennedy delivers a speech in Philadelphia expressing his gratitude for the city's support during the 1960 election, updating the audience on progress towards achieving his previously stated goals for America, and emphasizing the importance of continued economic growth and job creation.
