# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Fort_Lee
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This overview of Fort Lee, NJ, tells about its views of New York City, how to get to Fort Lee by car, bus, ferry or plane, and some of the attractions including Fort Lee Historic Park, a community center with dance, yoga and sports activities, some stores and international cuisine, such as pizzerias, delis, diners and Korean restaurants.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) Fort Lee is a diverse New Jersey city bordering the Hudson River and Manhattan via the George Washington Bridge, known for its Revolutionary War history, high-rise apartments, Korean cultural presence, international restaurants, and recreational parks offering spectacular views of the New York City skyline.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) Fort Lee in Bergen County boasts cultural diversity, a vibrant international dining scene, a significant Korean community, scenic NYC skyline views via the George Washington Bridge, and rich Revolutionary War history, along with parks, a lively town center, and excellent transportation, making it attractive to residents and visitors alike.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) Fort Lee is a city in Bergen County, New Jersey, known for its cultural diversity, convenient location, and stunning views of the Hudson River, with a range of amenities including parks, recreational facilities, and a variety of restaurants serving international cuisine.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Fort Lee, a diverse and densely populated city in Bergen County, New Jersey, is known for its proximity to the George Washington Bridge, cultural melting pot, scenic views, recreational spaces, and vibrant restaurant scene featuring international cuisines, particularly Korean.
# meta::title = Fort Lee
