# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Guadeloupe
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This guide lists attractions on each of the islands of Guadeloupe, a French overseas department in the Caribbean, focusing on places on the island of Grand Terre, including the economic capital Pointe-à-Pitre, the nightlife in Gosier, views from St François, the touristy city and beach of St Anne, cemetary of Morne à l'eau and other destinations around the islands.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) Guadeloupe, a French overseas department in the Caribbean known as “Butterfly Island,” consists of six main islands including Basse Terre, Grande Terre, Marie Galante, Les Saintes, La Désirade, and Petite Terre, offering visitors diverse attractions from volcanoes and waterfalls to beaches, rum distilleries, and vibrant nightlife.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) Guadeloupe, a French Caribbean territory, features diverse landscapes with lush vegetation and volcanic mountains, with key attractions including Carbet Falls, local rum distilleries, and vibrant nightlife in Pointe-à-Pitre and Gosier, alongside stunning beaches and cultural highlights.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) This overview of Guadeloupe, a French overseas department in the Caribbean, describes its geography, cities, attractions, and activities, including its islands, beaches, culture, and natural wonders like waterfalls and rum distilleries.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Guadeloupe, a French overseas department in the Caribbean, consists of multiple islands each offering unique landscapes and attractions such as lush mountains, beaches, and cultural experiences, with cities like Pointe-à-Pitre serving as economic hubs and Gosier providing nightlife options.
