# meta::sourceURL = https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Isfahan
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This guide to Isfahan, a beautiful ancient city in Iran, details its architectural sites such as the Safavid era Naqsh-e Jahan Square and Chaharbagh Boulevard, four stunning mosques and three palaces, and the Armenian Quarter (Jolfa), as well as transport information on airport and taxi connections.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) Isfahan, a historic Iranian city and former capital of Persia known as “Half The World,” features stunning Islamic architecture including the UNESCO-listed Naqsh-e Jahan Square, beautiful mosques adorned with intricate tiles, ancient palaces, and a unique Armenian Quarter established in the 1600s.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) Isfahan, in central Iran and a former Persian capital, is famous for its stunning Islamic architecture, including Imam and Sheikh Lotfollah Mosques, Ali Qapu Palace, and the UNESCO-listed Naqsh-e Jahan Square, and also has a vibrant Armenian Quarter and an international airport with regional flights.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) This article provides information about Isfahan, a city in central Iran known for its stunning architecture, beautiful streets, and historic mosques, including the famous Imam Mosque and Sheikh Lotfollah Mosque, and its many palaces and gardens, such as the Ali Qapu Palace and the Chehel Sotoun Palace.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) Isfahan, an ancient and culturally significant city in Iran with a rich history, boasts impressive architecture like the Naqsh-e Jahan Square and its iconic mosques, and serves as a major transportation hub connecting various regions of the country.
