# meta::summary1 = (human1) This guide to York, a Cathedral city in Yorkshire, England, with a population of 181,000, tells of its Roman and Viking era history, its renown for holding annual cultural festivals, and information about roads into the city, congested traffic and expensive parking.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) York is an ancient cathedral city in Northern England, founded by Romans in 71 CE and later ruled by Vikings, which now serves as a major tourist destination with rich historical heritage, numerous festivals, and well-preserved buildings, though driving into its center is discouraged.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) York in North Yorkshire, England, is a popular, family-friendly destination known for its well-preserved Roman heritage, vibrant cultural events like the Viking Festival, and status as England's second most visited city, with easy rail and road access, though city center driving is discouraged due to congestion and parking costs.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) This article provides an overview of York, a historic city in North Yorkshire, England, including its Roman history, Viking settlement, and modern attractions, as well as information on how to get to and around the city.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct; postedited) York, an ancient cathedral city with a population of over 181,000  and a rich history dating back to Roman times, boasts well-preserved historic buildings, hosts numerous cultural festivals throughout the year and attracts many visitors anually.
