# meta::summary1 = (human1) This basil growing guide recommends varieties (Cinnamon, Lemon, Purple, African Blue or Thai Basil), planting seed in containers with perlite, vermiculite, peat and soil before transfering sprouts to bigger containers or a garden, watering each morning and removing flower buds before plants bolt, and finally using basil for salads and pesto and freezing basil puree.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) This comprehensive guide to growing basil covers how to start from seeds indoors, transplant and care for the plants including watering and pest control, and harvest and store the leaves through fresh use, refrigeration, or freezing.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) This guide on growing basil outlines three key steps: starting seeds by selecting varieties and optimal planting conditions; caring for basil with proper soil, sunlight, and pest control while preventing flowering; and harvesting by pinching leaves to encourage growth, using fresh, and preserving by refrigerating or freezing pureed basil.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct; postedited) This article provides a three-part guide on how to grow basil, including starting seeds, caring for basil, and harvesting and using basil, covering topics such as soil preparation, watering, pruning, and pest control, as well as ways to store and use basil in various dishes.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) The article provides detailed instructions on growing basil, including choosing seeds, starting seeds indoors, transplanting, caring for mature plants, harvesting, and preserving the herb.
