# meta::salientEntities = 1 (5*), 2 (5*), 16 (5*), 17 (5*), 28 (5*), 29 (5*), 64 (5*), 3 (4*), 71 (4*), 7 (3*), 35 (3), 41 (3*), 11 (2*), 18 (2), 54 (2*), 58 (2), 79 (2), 84 (2*), 90 (2*), 92 (2*), 93 (2*), 14 (1), 42 (1*), 55 (1*), 72 (1), 89 (1*), 94 (1*)
# meta::sourceURL = https://www.wikihow.com/Annoy-People-in-Elevators
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This article suggests jokes and pranks to play on people in elevators, such as pushing all buttons, saying or singing 'ding' at every floor or announcing the floors, talking to your reflection in the mirror, standing in a corner facing the wall, dancing, putting a Lego city or Twister mat on the floor, or pretending to have lost a tarantula, snake or scorpion in the elevator.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) This guide to annoying people in elevators suggests pushing all floor buttons, making “ding” noises, talking to your reflection, facing the corner silently, dancing to elevator music, announcing floors loudly, claiming to have lost dangerous animals, building things inside, and making strange comments to fellow passengers.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) This guide suggests playful elevator pranks like pushing all buttons, making floor noises, dancing, announcing floors, pretending to lose a creature, building with Legos, laying a Twister mat, and having humorous chats, aiming for a lighthearted approach so everyone leaves with a fun story.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) This article provides tips on how to annoy people in elevators in a lighthearted and fun way, including pushing all the buttons, making loud noises, talking to your reflection, and dancing to elevator music.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) The article provides various lighthearted and amusing ways to prank people in elevators, including pushing multiple buttons, making noises, dancing, announcing floor numbers, pretending to lose a pet, and engaging in silly conversations or activities.
