# meta::sourceURL = https://www.wikihow.com/Flirt-Through-Instant-Messaging
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This guide to flirting via instant messaging suggests starting bu saying 'hi' and asking about someone's day, asking for help with work or school, or asking about their username, then moving on to musical likes and dislikes and making jokes, while avoiding self-deprecation, sappiness, excessive flattery or jokes at other people's expense.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) This article offers advice on flirting via instant messaging, recommending starting conversations casually with small talk and humor while avoiding being overly self-deprecating or sappy, and focusing on genuine engagement rather than excessive compliments.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) This guide advises starting casual, light conversations when flirting via instant message, avoiding prying or being overly self-deprecating, using humor to engage without relying on excessive compliments and prioritizing genuine interaction while respecting the other person's comfort and interests throughout.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) To flirt with someone online, start a conversation by asking about their day, work, or interests, and keep it light and fun, using humor and playful responses to build rapport, but avoid being too self-deprecating, sappy, or telling, and focus on having a genuine conversation.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) To effectively flirt via instant messaging, initiate with casual conversation, gradually introduce personal topics, use humor and authenticity, avoid self-deprecation or excessive sappiness, and build a genuine connection through shared interests and a natural flow.
