# meta::dateCreated = 2010-10-25
# meta::dateModified = 2015-09-15
# meta::genre = whow
# meta::salientEntities = 1 (5*), 18 (5*), 55 (5*), 4 (4*), 57 (4*), 7 (2), 39 (2*), 59 (2*), 60 (2*), 61 (2*), 102 (2), 104 (2), 3 (1), 19 (1*), 20 (1*), 33 (1), 40 (1*), 76 (1*), 78 (1*), 84 (1), 93 (1), 95 (1*), 98 (1), 103 (1), 108 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://www.wikihow.com/Make-a-Glowstick
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This guide to making a glowstick suggests using protective clothing and mixing hydrogen peroxide and water in one bowl, then luminol, sodium carbonate, copper sulfate, ammonium carbonate (available from websites such as Alfa Aesar or Sigma Aldrich) and water in another, and finally mixing some of both solutions in a bottle to create the glow.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) This guide explains how to make real glowsticks using luminol, which requires mixing specific amounts of hydrogen peroxide, distilled water, sodium carbonate, copper sulfate, and ammonium carbonate while using proper safety precautions, though the resulting glow only lasts a few minutes.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) The guide debunks Mountain Dew glowstick myths and offers a detailed tutorial using Luminol and other chemicals, also including safety tips, precise instructions, and warnings about the glow's short duration, humorously noting the difficulty of sourcing materials and suggesting easier lab methods.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) To make a glowstick without cheating, use a mixture of hydrogen peroxide, luminol, and other chemicals to create a glowing reaction, and follow a series of steps to mix and seal the solution, then wait for the glow to appear.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct; postedited) To make a glowstick without cheating, mix hydrogen peroxide and luminol solutions in sanitized containers, then shake and admire the brief glow, whereas for longer-lasting results suitable for parties, consider using more complex scientific methods requiring specialized equipment.
