# meta::sourceURL = https://www.wikihow.com/Pack-Your-Possessions-When-Moving
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This moving guide recommends packing each room, labeling and photographing what is in each box, filling sturdy boxes to the brim to allow for stacking, balancing heavy and light items so boxes can be lifted, marking fragile boxes and using bubble wrap or newspapers, getting free boxes from superstores (Walmart) and selling back boxes to U-haul.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) This guide on packing for a move advises organizing room by room, using sturdy boxes properly labeled and packed, protecting fragile items, keeping valuable items discreet, packing essentials separately, and includes tips on where to get boxes and how to document contents.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o; postedited) Organize packing by room and item frequency using sturdy, appropriately-sized boxes, securely tape and label, especially fragile items, create a first-night essentials box, balance heavy/light items, use discreet labels for valuables, get free boxes from stores, purchase extras if needed, and document, declutter, and designate a space for packed boxes in the new house.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) To pack your possessions when moving, start by labeling and organizing your belongings, packing heavy items first, and using sturdy boxes and bubble wrap for fragile items, and consider purchasing boxes in bulk from stores like Walmart or U-haul.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) The article provides detailed instructions on how to pack belongings during a move, emphasizing organization, labeling, proper boxing techniques, and safety measures to ensure a smooth relocation process.
# meta::title = How to Pack Your Possessions When Moving
