# newdoc id = GUM_whow_procrastinating
# global.Entity = GRP-etype-infstat-salience-centering-minspan-link-identity
# meta::author = Pranathi Kavuri, Adam Smith, Lillian Darnell and others (see URL)
# meta::dateCollected = 2016-09-19
# meta::dateCreated = 2006-03-14
# meta::dateModified = 2016-08-29
# meta::genre = whow
# meta::salientEntities = 11 (5*), 17 (5*), 59 (5*), 107 (4*), 15 (3*), 75 (3*), 76 (3*), 96 (3*), 1 (2*), 30 (2*), 47 (2*), 48 (2), 91 (2*), 114 (2), 4 (1), 5 (1), 9 (1), 20 (1), 21 (1*), 22 (1), 23 (1), 27 (1), 39 (1), 54 (1*), 57 (1*), 70 (1*), 81 (1*), 101 (1), 108 (1*)
# meta::sourceURL = https://www.wikihow.com/Stop-Procrastinating
# meta::speakerCount = 0
# meta::summary1 = (human1) This guide on preventing procrastination recommends using a prioritized to-do list with time frames, placed where you can see it, finishing hard stuff first or breaking it down into small parts you can accomplish today, using a timer ('time-boxing') and doing two-minute tasks whenever possible, or doing productive ten-minute work frenzies and ten-minute breaks.
# meta::summary2 = (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022) The article outlines strategies to overcome procrastination, including making detailed to-do lists, tackling hard tasks first, completing two-minute tasks immediately, using timed work intervals, and taking structured breaks to maintain productivity and focus.
# meta::summary3 = (gpt4o) This guide on overcoming procrastination suggests creating and managing a detailed to-do list, prioritizing tasks, tackling big projects early, addressing quick tasks immediately, using time-boxing techniques to boost productivity, and allowing yourself short breaks to refresh and refocus, all to cultivate motivation and reduce stress associated with delaying tasks.
# meta::summary4 = (Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct) To overcome chronic procrastination, create a to-do list, focus on the tasks you typically put off, set time-frames and deadlines, and use various productivity techniques such as the “two-minute task” rule, timed work frenzies, and time-boxing to stay focused and motivated.
# meta::summary5 = (Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) To overcome procrastination, create detailed to-do lists, prioritize tasks, write down ideas immediately, tackle large projects first, break big tasks into small steps, use timers, and take short breaks while ensuring deadlines are met.
# meta::title = How to Stop Procrastinating
